  d="NEGOTIATING TECH, BY NAME, ON GOOGLE'S AI OVERVIEW, SIGNED OUT, 2026-10-29: 'Negotiating a tech offer means treating the total compensation package—not just the base salary—as a flexible starting point.' Rules of negotiation, equity, sign-on bonus, start date, level, perks, leverage, and a closing request for the querent's own role and offers. Fourteen cards, the first the UC Berkeley Labor Center's 'Negotiating tech' (2 July 2025: 'This searchable inventory documents how unions have addressed workplace technologies through collective bargaining.'), the rest salary-negotiation advice.",
